# XWLightOS: /etc/environment must exist.
#
# The Seewo manager backend unit com.seewo.terminalmanager.service
# declares EnvironmentFile=/etc/environment WITHOUT the optional '-'
# prefix, so systemd refuses to start the service at all when this
# file is missing (no dash = missing file is a hard error, not a
# silent skip). The live image previously shipped no such file, which
# is a prime suspect for "manager backend autostart never comes up"
# (user report 2026-10-24): Restart=always would only spin a service
# that can never start. An empty file is a valid environment file.
#
# XWLightOS input method framework (user mail 2026-10-24 22:53: Shift
# toggle is a configuration problem, not an extension problem).
# Root cause of "config present but not effective": the IM variables
# previously lived ONLY in /etc/profile.d and /etc/X11/Xsession.d,
# which reach login shells and X11 sessions started via Xsession --
# but NOT a GDM-started GNOME session on its default path, and never
# a Wayland session. /etc/environment is read by pam_env for every
# display-manager login (X11 and Wayland alike) and by the systemd
# user manager, so it is the one channel guaranteed to reach the
# desktop session. Format here is VAR=value with no 'export' prefix
# (pam_env and systemd EnvironmentFile both require that form).
# The Xsession.d / profile.d copies stay as well (defense in depth).
GTK_IM_MODULE=fcitx
QT_IM_MODULE=fcitx
XMODIFIERS=@im=fcitx
#
# Qt theme (deep-chain fix, user mail 2026-10-24 22:40: font-color
# fixes keep not landing): Qt5 apps follow the GTK2 WhiteSur-Light
# theme only when QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=gtk2 reaches the session, but
# the profile.d copy is never sourced by a GDM-started GNOME session
# on its default path. Same pam_env channel as the IM variables above.
QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=gtk2
